"kw1106\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tuple</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>D, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range_reference_t\"><span class=\"kw2914\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range_rvalue_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>B<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">return</span> tuple<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>difference_type, Base<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i.<span class=\"me1\">pos_</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/ranges/iter_move\"><span class=\"kw3158\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iter_move</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i.<span class=\"me1\">current_</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></code></pre>\n<p>This function  is not visible to ordinary <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/unqualified_lookup\">unqualified</a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/qualified_lookup\">qualified lookup</a>, and can only be found by <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a> when <code>enumerate_view::<i>iterator</i>&lt;Const&gt;</code> is an associated class of the arguments.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> i\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> iterator\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A tuple that contains an index and the result of applying <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/ranges/iter_move\"><span class=\"kw3158\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iter_move</span></span></a></span></code> to the stored iterator.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-noexcept-full\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/noexcept_spec\"><code>noexcept</code></a> specification:&nbsp;&nbsp;\n<div class=\"t-noexcept-box\"><span class=\"t-cc\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><br>\n&n